@host = http://localhost:5276
@gateway = http://localhost:5299

### Log in as the customer (Petra) and paste accessToken below
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "petra@example.com", "password": "Customer123!" }

### Log in as the administrator and paste accessToken below
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@kofi.test", "password": "Admin123!" }

###
@customerToken = PASTE-CUSTOMER-TOKEN
@adminToken = PASTE-ADMIN-TOKEN
@orderId = REPLACE-WITH-ORDER-ID
@paymentId = REPLACE-WITH-PAYMENT-ID

### List products
GET {{host}}/products

### The catalogue is paged: page and pageSize (default 20, at most 100)
GET {{host}}/products?page=2&pageSize=5

### List products sorted by price
GET {{host}}/products?sort=price

### List customers
GET {{host}}/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Create an order
POST {{host}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Ada Lovelace",
  "street": "Botanicka 68a",
  "city": "Brno",
  "zip": "60200",
  "items": [
    { "productId": "REPLACE-WITH-PRODUCT-ID", "quantity": 2 }
  ]
}


### Pay an order (customer): the shop creates a payment at the provider and
### answers with its payment page. In a browser you would go to redirectUrl.
POST {{host}}/orders/{{orderId}}/pay
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Without a browser: press "Pay" on the provider's page
POST {{gateway}}/payments/{{paymentId}}/approve

### The provider sends the browser back here; the shop asks the provider
### for the payment's status before it marks the order paid
GET {{host}}/orders/{{orderId}}/payment-return?paymentId={{paymentId}}

### My order (customer): only your own, anyone else's is 404
GET {{host}}/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### KOFI-118: stock is reserved even though the order fails
### (first item is in stock, second one is not — check the stock of the
###  first product before and after)
POST {{host}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Ada Lovelace",
  "street": "Botanicka 68a",
  "city": "Brno",
  "zip": "60200",
  "items": [
    { "productId": "REPLACE-WITH-V60-ID", "quantity": 1 },
    { "productId": "REPLACE-WITH-GRINDER-ID", "quantity": 999 }
  ]
}

### Get order detail (price breakdown, recalculated)
GET {{host}}/orders/REPLACE-WITH-ORDER-ID
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### The same OrderDto goes in and comes out.
### Status, total, the e-mail and the item prices below are ignored on the way in —
### the server decides them. Nothing tells you that.
POST {{host}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "customerName": "Ada Lovelace",
  "customerEmail": "ada@example.com",
  "street": "Botanicka 68a",
  "city": "Brno",
  "zip": "60200",
  "status": "Shipped",
  "total": 99999,
  "items": [
    { "productId": "REPLACE-WITH-PRODUCT-ID", "quantity": 2, "unitPrice": 1, "productName": "whatever" }
  ]
}

### And the list returns that same shape with itemsTotal, shipping and
### items empty, because only the detail bothers to fill them in.
GET {{host}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### List orders
GET {{host}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### The same list, the way the admin screen calls it
GET {{host}}/orders?onlyPaid=true&includeItems=true&sortBy=total
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Three ways to fail
### 1) 400 with { error: ... }
POST {{host}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerName": "X", "items": [] }

### 2) 500 with a plain string
POST {{host}}/orders/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 3) unhandled exception
POST {{host}}/orders/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/ship
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### No validation anywhere: empty name, invalid e-mail, 201 Created
POST {{host}}/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "", "email": "not-an-email" }
